infographic compare-quadrant-quarter-simple-card
data
  title At the TTL boundary: wait vs DB load
  desc Two axes — user wait (zero / nonzero) and DB queries (one / N concurrent)
  compares
    - label SWR & XFetch — zero wait, one query
      desc Stale served instantly to all; exactly one background rebuild. The goal quadrant.
    - label Naive TTL — zero wait, N queries
      desc No one waits, but all N requests hit the DB at once and it falls over.
    - label Lock & single-flight — wait, one query
      desc DB load is 1, but waiters queue up to the rebuild p99 before they get a value.
    - label Worst case — wait and N queries
      desc Nonzero wait with an unprotected DB; no mitigation lives here by design.
theme
  palette #10b981 #f59e0b #6366f1 #f43f5e
